From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] platform_thread_types: Only include asm/unistd_64.h on
 x86_64

Upstream includes <asm/unistd_64.h> on every non-ARM Linux target, but that
header does not exist on most other architectures (MIPS, RISC-V, s390x,
PowerPC, LoongArch, ...), and on 32-bit x86 it would redefine __NR_gettid
with the 64-bit syscall number. <sys/syscall.h> already provides the right
definition everywhere, so restrict the include to x86_64 (LP64).
---
diff --git a/webrtc/rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc b/webrtc/rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc
index b521f61..c72ca2c 100644
--- a/webrtc/rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc
+++ b/webrtc/rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #include <sys/prctl.h>
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 
-#if !defined(WEBRTC_ARCH_ARM) && !defined(WEBRTC_ARCH_ARM64)
+#if defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__ILP32__)
 #include <asm/unistd_64.h>
 #endif
 #endif
-- 
2.49.0

